1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,240
Luke 14

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:07,980
One Sabbath, when he went to dine at the house of a ruler of the Pharisees,

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,700
they were watching him carefully.

4
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:13,920
And behold, there was a man before him who had dropsy.

5
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,340
And Jesus responded to the lawyers and Pharisees, saying,

6
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:20,940
Is it lawful to heal on the Sabbath, or not?

7
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,820
But they remained silent.

8
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:26,360
Then he took him and healed him and sent him away.

9
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,000
And he said to them,

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,860
Which of you, having a son or an ox that has fallen into a well on a Sabbath day,

11
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:36,000
will not immediately pull him out?

12
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,800
And they could not reply to these things.

13
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:42,780
Now he told a parable to those who were invited when he noticed

14
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:46,260
how they chose the places of honor, saying to them,

15
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,760
When you are invited by someone to a wedding feast,

16
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,420
do not sit down in a place of honor,

17
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:55,760
lest someone more distinguished than you be invited by him,

18
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,840
and he who invited you both will come,

19
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:58,860
and say to you,

20
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,040
Give your place to this person,

21
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:04,680
and then you will begin with shame to take the lowest place.

22
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,680
But when you are invited,

23
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:09,000
go and sit in the lowest place,

24
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,740
so that when your host comes he may say to you,

25
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:13,960
Friend, move up higher.

26
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:18,140
Then you will be honored in the presence of all who sit at table with you.

27
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,500
For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled,

28
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,220
and he who humbles himself will be exalted.

29
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:27,980
He said also to the man who had invited him,

30
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:30,500
When you give a dinner or a banquet,

31
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,880
do not invite your friends or your brothers,

32
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,780
or your relatives or rich neighbors,

33
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:38,140
lest they also invite you in return and you be repaid.

34
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,140
But when you give a feast,

35
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:43,900
invite the poor, the crippled, the lame, the blind,

36
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:45,800
and you will be blessed,

37
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:47,700
because they cannot repay you.

38
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:51,720
For you will be repaid at the resurrection of the just.

39
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:55,720
When one of those who reclined at table with him heard these things,

40
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:56,840
he said to him,

41
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:57,960
Blessed!

42
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:01,320
Blessed is everyone who will eat bread in the kingdom of God.

43
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:02,320
But he said to him,

44
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:06,320
A man once gave a great banquet and invited many.

45
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:10,320
And at the time for the banquet he sent his servant to say to those who had been invited,

46
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:13,320
Come, for everything is now ready.

47
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:16,320
But they all alike began to make excuses.

48
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,320
The first said to him,

49
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:21,320
I have bought a field, and I must go out and see it.

50
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:23,320
Please have me excused.

51
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,320
And another said,

52
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,320
I have bought five yoke of oxen,

53
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,320
and I go to examine them.

54
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,600
Please have me excused.

55
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,720
And another said,

56
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:35,640
I have married a wife, and therefore I cannot come.

57
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:39,640
So the servant came and reported these things to his master.

58
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:42,560
Then the master of the house became angry and said to his servant,

59
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:46,200
Go out quickly to the streets and lanes of the city,

60
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:49,320
and bring in the poor and crippled, and blind and lame.

61
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,320
And the servant said,

62
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:55,400
Sir, what you commanded has been done, and still there is room.

63
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:55,640
And the master said to him,

64
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,840
And the master said to the servant,

65
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:02,300
Go out to the highways and hedges, and compel people to come in,

66
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,560
that my house may be filled.

67
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:09,520
For I tell you, none of those men who were invited shall taste my banquet.

68
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:14,840
Now great crowds accompanied him, and he turned and said to them,

69
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:19,560
If anyone comes to me and does not hate his own father and mother,

70
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:22,600
and wife and children and brothers and sisters,

71
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:25,460
yes, and even his own life,

72
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:27,300
he cannot be my disciple.

73
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:31,420
Whoever does not bear his own cross and come after me

74
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:33,340
cannot be my disciple.

75
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:37,440
For which of you, desiring to build a tower,

76
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,100
does not first sit down and count the cost,

77
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:42,180
whether he has enough to complete it?

78
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:46,020
Otherwise, when he has laid a foundation and is not able to finish,

79
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:48,980
all who see it begin to mock him, saying,

80
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:52,680
This man began to build and was not able to finish.

81
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,540
Or what king, going out to encounter

82
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:55,620
a man who was not able to finish,

83
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:56,680
or another king in war,

84
00:03:57,080 --> 00:04:00,820
will not sit down first and deliberate whether he is able with ten thousand

85
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:03,680
to meet him who comes against him with twenty thousand?

86
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:07,340
And if not, while the other is yet a great way off,

87
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:10,620
he sends a delegation and asks for terms of peace.

88
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:16,020
So therefore, any one of you who does not renounce all that he has

89
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:17,720
cannot be my disciple.

90
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:22,620
Salt is good, but if salt has lost its taste,

91
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:24,920
how shall its saltiness be restored?

92
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:29,060
It is of no use either for the soil or for the manure pile.

93
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:30,660
It is thrown away.

94
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:35,340
He who has ears to hear, let him hear.

